// Eternalize [CR#702.129a]: "Eternalize [cost]" means "[cost], Exile this card
// from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a 4/4
// black Zombie. Eternalize only as a sorcery." Embalm's bigger twin
// ([CR#702.128a]): same activated-from-graveyard, exile-self, sorcery-speed
// shell; the token copy is 4/4 and black rather than keeping its P/T and being
// white.
//
// Pieces (all over existing primitives — no engine gap):
//   - from / cost / window: identical to Embalm/Scavenge — activate from the
//     graveyard, printed [cost] then `Do(Move(This, Exile))` spliced flat, only
//     as a sorcery ([CR#602.5d]).
//   - effect: `Create(agent: You, count: 1, token: Copy(source: SelfCard, ...))` — a token copy of the
//     exiled card ([CR#707.1]) EXCEPT it's 4/4 (`Power(Set(4))` + `Toughness(Set(4))`,
//     [CR#707.9d]), black (`Colors(Set([Black]))`), and a Zombie in addition to
//     its other types (`Subtypes(Add(Zombie))`). No mana cost needs no
//     exception (a token has no mana-cost slot, [CR#111.3,707.2]).
(
    name: "Eternalize",
    template: "eternalize ${0}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: [Cost],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Eternalize",
        abilities: [Activated(
            from: Graveyard,
            cost: [Splice(Param(0)), Do(Move(This, Exile))],
            window: SorcerySpeed,
            effect: Create(agent: You, count: 1, token: Copy(source: SelfCard, exceptions: [
                Modify(Power(Set(4))),
                Modify(Toughness(Set(4))),
                Modify(Colors(Set([Black]))),
                Modify(Subtypes(Add(Zombie))),
            ])),
        )],
    ),
)
